The '''Protectors Camp''' was the base of operations for the [[Journeyman Protector|Mandalorian Protectors]], a group of [[Mandalorian]] warriors sworn to defend the [[Concord Dawn system]]. It was built on the [[Third moon of Concord Dawn|third moon]] of the [[planet]] [[Concord Dawn]] and led by [[Fenn Rau]].<ref name="Protectors Camp DB">{{Databank|the-protectors-camp|The Protectors Camp}}</ref>

==History==
During the [[Imperial Era]], the Protectors maintained a base on [[Concord Dawn]]'s [[Third moon of Concord Dawn|third moon]] in order defend the system.<ref name="Protectors Camp DB" /> In [[3 BBY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of "[[The Protector of Concord Dawn]]" to [[3 BBY]].</ref> following a [[Dogfight over Concord Dawn|dogfight]] with the [[Early rebellion against the Galactic Empire|Rebels]]' [[Phoenix Squadron]], Rau met with an [[Unidentified Imperial officer (Concord Dawn)|Imperial officer]] that gave him credits as promised in their agreement. Rau also informed the officer of his encounter with a Rebel squadron and the officer told Rau to notify him if the rebels return.<ref name="The Protector of Concord Dawn" />

During this time, the base was [[Mission to the third moon of Concord Dawn|infiltrated]] by two rebels, Jedi [[Kanan Jarrus]] and [[Sabine Wren]]. As Jarrus spoke with Rau about him saving his and Master [[Depa Billaba]]'s life during the [[Third Battle of Mygeeto|Third Battle]] of [[Mygeeto]], Wren then planted explosives on the [[Fang-class Protectorate fighter|Fang fighters]]. However, several of the Protectors found Wren and assumed she was a bounty hunter. Wren, as a member of [[House Vizsla]]'s [[Clan Wren]], demanded a duel with Rau in accordance to the [[Mandalorian code]]. Rau then agreed to it, despite Jarrus telling Sabine that this was not what [[Hera Syndulla|Hera]] wanted. However, Sabine then set off the charges and destroyed most of the Fang fighters. Rau and his protectors then attempted to capture the rebels, but the rebels escaped and Rau was taken prisoner by the Rebels. Due to his status, Rau then told his protectors to allow the Rebels passage through the system and not to mention his capture to the Empire.<ref name="The Protector of Concord Dawn" />

